Seven Wonders Engine — source origin and licensing

Derived from DMAG/UFSM's 7Wonders simulator:
https://github.com/dmag-ufsm/7Wonders
Upstream baseline: a0bc333a7a7f21f83156de8a2d522e7baa913f0a (2021-10-07).

Downstream modifications maintained by Marten Krohn include selectable-resource
corrections, Gizah B's fourth-stage transition, seeded RNG, protocol v2,
atomic status publication, final scoring status, resource-allocation reset,
status calculation optimizations, regression tests and standalone packaging.
See docs/ORIGIN.md and docs/SIMULATOR_CHANGES.md for scope and exact evidence.
The initial standalone extraction is dated 2026-11-05; it changes packaging,
not game data or rules. The original engine is not claimed as newly authored.

The original GNU GPL version 3 LICENSE is retained. Distribution is under
GPL-3.0-only. The upstream README's MIT sentence conflicts with its explicit
LICENSE; this fork follows the supplied GPLv3 license. Vendored
include/nlohmann/ headers retain Niels Lohmann and contributors' MIT notices.

No rights in board-game names, trademarks, publisher artwork or BGA assets
are claimed. This is an unofficial project with no publisher/BGA affiliation.
The current checkout excludes upstream GUI artwork and RL experiment data;
unmodified upstream history remains accessible through the fork.

2026-11-05: The optional original Tk GUI is restored in gui/legacy_view.py,
with a downstream launcher, protocol coordinator and compatibility corrections.
It derives from the original Game.py at the baseline above. Artwork remains
external. The C++ rules and build files are unchanged by this restoration.
